Q: Need help using ((ImageView) findViewById.getView().(R.id.imageView1)).setImageBitmap(bmp); in a fragment A: <p>If you are in a fragment then I would advise you to to your assignment in the <code>onCreateView</code>method after creating your view for your fragment:</p>
<pre><code>public View onCreateView(final LayoutInflater inflater, final ViewGroup container, final Bundle savedInstanceState) {
        final View rootView = inflater.inflate(R.layout.fragment_layout, container, false);
        Bitmap bmp;//&lt;= retrieve/create your bitmap here
        ImageView image =((ImageView) rootView.findViewById(R.id.imageView1));
        image.setImageBitmap(bmp);
        return rootView;
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to type-hint a function that returns as many values as in its input? A: <p>You need to make <code>val2</code> positional only:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>from typing import overload

@overload
def foo(val: int) -&gt; str: ...

@overload
def foo(val: int, val2: int, /, *more_vals: int) -&gt; tuple[str, ...]: ...

def foo(val: int, *more_vals: int) -&gt; str | tuple[str, ...]:
    out = tuple(str(v) for v in (val, *more_vals))
    if not more_vals:
        (out,) = out
    return out
</code></pre>
<p>Otherwise something like <code>foo(1, val2=2)</code> would be allowed by the overload but not the actual implementation</p>

